fda-med-device pack: content licence
====================================

This pack is derived from the thirteen sources listed below (rows S1 to S12 plus
S4a of the source-vetting record). Their landing-page URLs are held in the build
spec dated 2026-09-24 and are not reproduced here; the repository link policy
bans source-material hosts (see ../../docs/LICENSING.md).

Source licence: Public Domain (US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105)  (tier 1; see
../../docs/SOURCE-VETTING.md). No source-material download link is published.

The guidance documents and the final rule are works of the United States
Government prepared by FDA staff, and are NOT subject to copyright protection in
the United States (17 U.S.C. 105). They are in the public domain: anyone may
reproduce, transform, and redistribute them for any purpose, including
commercially, without permission. Material published on fda.gov, including the
QMSR overview page (S4a), is covered by the FDA Website Policies statement,
"Linking to or Copying Information":

    "Unless otherwise noted, the contents of the FDA website (www.fda.gov) — both
     text and graphics — are not copyrighted. They are in the public domain and
     may be republished, reprinted and otherwise used freely by anyone."

Federal regulations and Federal Register rule text (S4, S5) are US Government
works under the same statute.

Attribution to FDA is provided as a courtesy (see the repository NOTICE), not as
a legal obligation. FDA does not endorse this pack or its authors.

Each source below carries a vetting block: exact title, pinned date, docket or
FR document where known, licence basis, what the pack reconstructs from it, and
the chapters that use it. Items marked "confirmed from PDF" were checked against
the local source-text captures on 2026-09-24; where a docket is printed only on
the FDA landing page and not in the PDF, the landing-page value is pinned.

Reconstruction: all pack content is synthesized reference notes in the authors'
own words. Quotations are limited to short passages (two-sentence cap per quote,
enforced by the pack gates). The documents themselves are not republished here.

NOTE: This file governs the CONTENT of this pack. The repository tooling is
licensed separately under MIT (see ../../LICENSE).


THE THIRTEEN SOURCES
====================

S1  Content of Premarket Submissions for Device Software Functions
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH)   Issued: 2023-06-14   Status: Final   Docket: FDA-2021-D-0775
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Supersedes: "Guidance for the Content of Premarket Submissions for Software
    Contained in Medical Devices" (May 2005), per its cover page.
    Reconstructs: the Basic and Enhanced documentation levels, the level-of-concern
    driver, and the premarket software documentation elements.
    Used in: ch01, ch02

S2  General Principles of Software Validation
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH, CBER)   Issued: 2002-01-11 (Version 2.0)   Status: Final
    Docket: FDA-1997-D-0029 (landing page)
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Superseded in part: Section 6, "Validation of Automated Process Equipment and
    Quality System Software," is superseded by S3 (confirmed from the S3 PDF text,
    2026-09-24); the remaining sections stay in force and are used here.
    Reconstructs: validation principles, lifecycle software validation activities,
    validation of changes, independence, and record expectations.
    Used in: ch01, ch03, ch04

S3  Computer Software Assurance for Production and Quality Management System Software
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH, CBER)   Issued: 2026-02-03   Status: Final   Docket: FDA-2022-D-0795
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Supersedes: "Computer Software Assurance for Production and Quality System
    Software," issued 2025-09-24 (confirmed from PDF). Supplements S2 except that
    it supersedes Section 6 of S2, "Validation of Automated Process Equipment and
    Quality System Software" (confirmed from PDF, 2026-09-24).
    Reconstructs: risk-based assurance for production and QMS software, intended-use
    determination, assurance-activity selection, and record content.
    Used in: ch01, ch04

S4  Medical Devices; Quality System Regulation Amendments (final rule)
    Publisher: FDA (HHS)   Published: 2024-02-02   Effective: 2026-02-02   Status: Final rule
    Citation: 89 FR 7496 (start page confirmed from the rule text header: Vol. 89,
    No. 23, Friday, February 2, 2024; the rule runs to p. 7523)
    FR Doc. 2024-01709   Docket: FDA-2021-N-0507   RIN: 0910-AH99
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Reconstructs: what the QMSR change did to 21 CFR part 820, the incorporation by
    reference of ISO 13485:2016, FDA-specific additions retained outside ISO 13485,
    and the transition timeline. Summarised as obligations in FDA's words; no ISO
    text is reproduced.
    Used in: ch01, ch05

S4a Quality Management System Regulation (QMSR), FDA overview page
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH)   Web page   Fetched: 2026-09-24
    Basis: FDA Website Policies public-domain statement (quoted above)
    Reconstructs: the effective date and the incorporation-by-reference scope as
    FDA states them for readers, cross-checked against S4.
    Used in: ch01, ch05

S5  eCFR 21 CFR Part 820, Quality Management System Regulation (current text)
    Publisher: Office of the Federal Register (eCFR)   Regulation
    Text currency: Title 21 "up to date as of 9/22/2026," last amended 9/22/2026
    (per the eCFR capture header); retrieved 2026-09-24
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Reconstructs: the structure and obligations of the current Part 820 as amended
    by S4. Summarised, not republished; section numbers only.
    Used in: ch01, ch05

S6  Cybersecurity in Medical Devices: Quality Management System Considerations
    and Content of Premarket Submissions
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH, CBER)   Issued: 2026-02-03   Status: Final   Docket: FDA-2021-D-1158
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Supersedes: "Cybersecurity in Medical Devices: Quality System Considerations
    and Content of Premarket Submissions," issued 2025-06-27 (confirmed from PDF).
    Reconstructs: the secure product development framework, threat modelling,
    cybersecurity risk management, security architecture views, SBOM content and
    placement, cybersecurity labelling, and postmarket vulnerability management.
    Used in: ch01, ch06, ch07, ch09

S7  Clinical Decision Support Software
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH, CBER)   Issued: 2026-01-29   Status: Final
    Docket: FDA-2017-D-6569 (recorded from the PDF cover page)
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Supersedes: "Clinical Decision Support Software," issued 2026-01-06 (per its
    cover page).
    Reconstructs: the four statutory criteria for non-device CDS as the 2026
    guidance reads them, and the boundary cases and worked examples.
    Used in: ch01, ch11

S8  Off-The-Shelf Software Use in Medical Devices
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH)   Issued: 2023-08-11   Status: Final   Docket: FDA-2019-D-3598
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Originally issued: 1999-09-09; the 2023 final supersedes the 1999 guidance
    (per its cover page).
    Reconstructs: OTS/SOUP documentation, the risk-based level of verification and
    validation evidence, and maintenance and obsolescence expectations.
    Used in: ch01, ch08

S9  Deciding When to Submit a 510(k) for a Software Change to an Existing Device
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH, CBER)   Issued: 2017-10-25   Status: Final   Docket: FDA-2016-D-2021
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Reconstructs: the change-assessment flowchart logic, its question sequence,
    and how a no-510(k) decision is documented.
    Used in: ch01, ch10

S10 Medical Device Data Systems, Medical Image Storage Devices, and Medical Image
    Communications Devices
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH)   Issued: 2022-09-28   Status: Final   Docket: FDA-2014-D-0798
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Originally issued: 2015-02-09 (per its cover page).
    Reconstructs: the MDDS and image-storage/communications function categories
    and how the 21st Century Cures software provisions moved them outside the
    device definition.
    Used in: ch01, ch08

S11 Electronic Submission Template for Medical Device 510(k) Submissions
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH)   Issued: 2023-10-02   Status: Final   Docket: FDA-2021-D-0872
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    Originally issued: 2022-09-22; eSTAR 510(k) submissions mandatory from
    2023-10-01 (per the guidance and landing page).
    Reconstructs: the eSTAR 510(k) template structure and what it enforces for
    software and cybersecurity content.
    Used in: ch01, ch12

S12 Electronic Submission Template for Medical Device De Novo Requests
    Publisher: FDA (CDRH)   Issued: 2024-08-23   Status: Final
    Docket: FDA-2023-D-3788 (recorded from the PDF cover page)
    Basis: US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105
    eSTAR De Novo submissions mandatory from 2025-10-01 (per the landing page).
    Reconstructs: the eSTAR De Novo template structure and its mandatory date.
    Used in: ch01, ch12


EXCLUDED MATERIAL (cited by name only; no text reproduced)
=========================================================

The following standards are copyrighted and are NOT licensed to this pack. The
pack names them and describes FDA's own obligations only; it reproduces no
standard text, table, or clause wording.

-   ISO 13485:2016, "Medical devices: Quality management systems. Requirements
    for regulatory purposes." Incorporated by reference into 21 CFR 820 by S4; the
    incorporation changes the regulatory status of the standard, not its
    copyright.
-   ISO 9000:2015, "Quality management systems: Fundamentals and vocabulary"
    (clause 3 vocabulary is incorporated by reference alongside ISO 13485:2016).
-   ISO 14971, "Medical devices: Application of risk management to medical devices."
-   IEC 62304, "Medical device software: Software life cycle processes."

These exclusions and the cleared status of S1 to S12 plus S4a are recorded in
../../docs/SOURCE-VETTING.md.
